  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Negate the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ Some composite numbers are not divisible by $3.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $C$ be the set of all composite numbers. The given statement can be re-phrased as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists $x\\in C$ such that $x$ is not divisible by $3.$\n\nIntroducing the existential quantifier, we get the following:\n\n$\\,$ $∃x\\in C,\\,x\\text{ is not divisible by }3.$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∃x\\in C,\\,x\\text{ is not divisible by }3) & ≡∀x\\in C,\\,¬(x\\text{ is not divisible by }3) \\\\  & ≡∀x\\in C,\\,x\\text{ is divisible by }3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich reads \n\n$\\,$ For all $x\\in C,$ $x\\text{ is divisible by }3.$\n\nor simply\n\n$\\,$ All composite numbers are divisible by $3.$",
